{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543883-would-you-allow-a-mage-to-do-that","id":1543883,"title":"Would you allow a Mage to do that!?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-15T10:06:16-07:00","id":1543883,"title":"Would you allow a Mage to do that!?","content":"So, here I am again with some crazy question trying to see what other fellow Mage players and Storytellers alike think.<br /> <br /> As I have posted here many times, I'm a Storyteller with about 20 years of experieence with the game, I've been a storyteller since I was a child, at first because I noticed my friends were both not very good at it or didn't seem to like the idea of being a storyteller that much (probably both things combined, as both are linked). So I ended up loving it since I was very young and now I'm funny enough more open to crazy ideas my players come up with for stories. I also love crossovers and as such a player of mine came up with a very crazy idea, because he loves &quot;a certain vampire&quot; and his mage character came up with something I felt very, I mean very relutant to even bother considering. He wants to know if it would be possible to make a ward to protect his vampire lover from the sunlight, yes you read that right, he wants to ward the vampire against one of the banes of a vampire existence. I'm naturally, totally, utterly against such idea, but he wanted me to consult other fellow storytellers and here I am. What do you guys think of this absurd idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T10:29:29-07:00","id":1543886,"title":"","content":"I would say sure. Its na easy forces 2 effect, but the vamp would always look like standing in the shade so would often break the mascarade and generate paradox. This would not directly break the curse and create its own problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T10:39:16-07:00","id":1543888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543883-would-you-allow-a-mage-to-do-that?p=1543886#post1543886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say sure. Its na easy forces 2 effect, but the vamp would always look like standing in the shade so would often break the mascarade and generate paradox. This would not directly break the curse and create its own problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting is in the 16th century, we're using sorcere's crusade and I'm allowing currently mages and vampires in the story. So the masquerade isn't really a thing and &quot;paradox&quot; is a bit different. I wouldn't see any problem in that if it was for a scene/day even, but the intention is to kind of enchant his vampiric lover's body to be warded against sunlight ( I even joked saying that then I'd make the vampire in question vunlerable to shadows and darkness to offset that lol). What concerns me is the complexity of the feat, depending on the interpretation it could be accomplished like you said, like offering a kind of shadow cover for the vampire, it would be a bit complexxt to make it walk with the vampire, but still, even though very strange, it should be possible. What I feel would be much harder is the fact that he wants to give the vampire a prolongued (if I'd allowed him, I bet he would even try permanent one lol) protection as if enchanting the vampire's own skin to be impervious to the Sun. It naturally has MANY and MUCH DEEPER implications as vampires were cursed by God, so how would one be able to make her skin immune to the effects of such curse...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T12:02:15-07:00","id":1543899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543883-would-you-allow-a-mage-to-do-that#post1543883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He wants to know if it would be possible to make a ward to protect his vampire lover from the sunlight, yes you read that right, he wants to ward the vampire against one of the banes of a vampire existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not totally unheard of<br /> Corpse in the Monster&quot; the 5th level power called &quot;Gift of Life&quot; allows the necromancer to transform into a human-life state. Taking no damage to the sun, being able to eat, have sex, drink and pretty much do anything that humans enjoy.<br /> With Mytherceria's&quot;The Grandest Trick&quot;, the Kiasyd making themselves/the universe believe that they were never nor have ever been a vampire<br /> Serpentis' Pact with Ra allowy the Followr of Set by &quot;remindig Ra&quot; Sutekh was his champion to walk in the sun without harm for one day<br /> <br /> Even clan curses are possible to overcome<br /> Martinelli's Ring of Clear Thought is a vampiric artifact from The Players Guide to the Sabbat, p. 154 ('92 edition)<br /> A ghoul created it for her as a gift for her Malkavian Master. Wearing the ring removes all fears, phobias, derangements, and any mental flaws the individual wearing the ring might have. Removing the ring brings them back twice as strong, and the wearer becomes obsessed with recovering it.<br /> <br /> Not to mention any demonic investments and dark pacts... <br /> <br /> So the means is there to remove the pesky Sun-problem... for a Mage, especially in the 16th century creating an artifact, medalion or ring that protects the wearer should be possible - not an easy feat tho'<br /> More so the Curse - if you going by the Book of Nod is not from God but from Raphael - the driver of the Sun, ward of the East<br /> His curse according the Book of Nod was &quot;For as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will fear the dawn, and the sun's rays will seek to burn you like fire where ever you hide always&quot;<br /> <br /> So technically your Mage needs to protect the Vampire in question from an Archangle's &quot;curse&quot; and if you are goning by the word interpretation then the Sun's rays burn like fire - give her immunity to fire and problem solved so to speak (cheap cop out)<br /> Or like with Mytherceria's&quot;The Grandest Trick &quot;fool&quot; the universe to ignore the Vampire is a Vampire<br /> <br /> I think you could wave an amusing and amazing story around the Mage and the Vampire and how they try to find a way to escape this part of the curse - but you should deffinitly let them to try<br /> After all, there are many instances (even sufficiently high Fortitude actually enough) when the Sun is not that a big problem...<br /> <i>Studying </i>these instances and methods and figure out a way - even maybe bargain with Raphael himself (The Salubri's &quot;<b>Blessing of the Name</b>&quot; is the &quot;proof&quot; Angels exist in Vampire/WoD, the Salubri with that power invoke the angel whose name she shares and specify what she wishes to use it for , essentially a petition to the member of the Havenly Host... and it <i>works </i>,) - they eventually could find a way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T12:35:16-07:00","id":1543902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the intention is to kind of enchant his vampiric lover's body to be warded against sunlight ( I even joked saying that then I'd make the vampire in question vunlerable to shadows and darkness to offset that lol).</div> </div> </div> </div>The new True Black Hand book does suggest something like this is what would happen overtime if magick it's abused to this very end. The Curse mutates if it's foiled creating new weaknesses - it's an interesting way to deal with this sort of things, a bit &quot;party pooper&quot; but not the worst. It defines the Curse as an almost &quot;smart&quot; foe, or at least much more complex than what meets the eye <br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> Wards work by impeding two things from ever coming into contact. A total ward against sunlight (forbidding the sun to ever touch his loved) would make the vampire a patch of absolute darkness (or invisible, if the light just passes through), only becoming visible when there's another source of ligth (like fire)<br /> <br /> Sunligth &quot;immunity&quot; wouldn't be a ward. And that would require to make changes of the Vampires pattern, it's nature. Due to the Cosmological Constants it's justifiable to say it's impossible.<br /> <br /> BUT, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Shadeprowler</a> points out. If it's just being able to fend off sunligth, it isn't that unheard off, and just saying no it's boring. It could be better to encourage to seek &quot;loopholes&quot; to the prohibition, or negotiate it somehow. It should be clarified that this feat goes somewhat outside of the normal rules used for run-of-the-mill everyday spells, and may invoke extraordinary rules or limitations depending on the method imagined.<br /> <br /> I would say, in any case, that enchanting the vampire itself would cost Permanent Scourge (that rule did exist on Cruzade, if I remember correctly) to the mage while the spell it's active, not unlike raising Atributes above 5 or wanting to be immortal. Having Vulgar stuff that's &quot;always&quot; active it's the kind of thing that justifies this sort of marks - and you ARE raising your middle finger to God, after all.<br /> <br /> Relegating the ward or transformation to an item could deviate the Scourge, with the caveat of making the object itself a potential weakness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-15-2024, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T12:55:03-07:00","id":1543903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Corpse in the Monster&quot; the 5th level power called &quot;Gift of Life&quot; allows the necromancer to transform into a human-life state. Taking no damage to the sun, being able to eat, have sex, drink and pretty much do anything that humans enjoy. </div> </div> </div>Yes, <i>Benedicto Vitae</i> is a very intersting power, although I'd say it would perhaps fits better into a ritual than into a path Power. I've always wondered myself if one vampire could conceive a child using this power and this was asked by the same player who wanted to have a baby between his mage and his vampire lover.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to mention any demonic investments and dark pacts... </div> </div> </div>Yes, with <i>Blasphemous Pact</i> from <i>Tome of Secrets</i> a vampire can even breed and it's stated clearly in the merit's text, so I could see a vampire using this merit to ignore one of the curses of being a vampire with no big problem, besides the obvious and deadly consequences of being an infernalist ofc lol (I once even had a player who wanted to use this merit to have his vampire use True Magick, stating that he would ask to have his Avatar restored somehow, however unholy it was and then I told him it would be easier for him to use the power <i>Chain the Enlightened</i> from A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra and have a mage be his <i>Blood Familiar </i>if he really felt the need for his vampire to use True Magick in the game as it would save me the headache of having a Vampire with an Avatar performing True Magick in my game, at least with <i>Chain the Enlightened</i> the metaphysical explanation is already there and it's satisfatory enough, I didn't want to have to create another, so I said no)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More so the Curse - if you going by the Book of Nod is not from God but from Raphael - the driver of the Sun, ward of the East </div> </div> </div>We could argue of whether the curse came originally from Raphael or if he was merely the &quot;messenger&quot;, but that would be a whole another discussion in itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you could wave an amusing and amazing story around the Mage and the Vampire and how they try to find a way to escape this part of the curse - but you should deffinitly let them to try </div> </div> </div>Yes, I deep inside feel this urge to let them try, because &quot;why not&quot;. Also, I need to add that Sunlight is systematically very different from Fire, so I'd never allow any fire immunity to grant a vampire immunity to Sunlight, they are very different and treatd as such through dozens of powers and systems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (The Salubri's &quot;<b>Blessing of the Name</b>&quot; is the &quot;proof&quot; Angels exist in Vampire/WoD, the Salubri with that power invoke the angel whose name she shares and specify what she wishes to use it for , essentially a petition to the member of the Havenly Host... and it <i>works </i>, </div> </div> </div>I honstely felt that at this point I knew every single Vampire/Mage/Werewolf/Changeling/Fae power in the game, but I don't recall this &quot;Blessing of the Name&quot;, where can I find information about it? Is it in Clanbook Salubri?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T13:12:22-07:00","id":1543905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543883-would-you-allow-a-mage-to-do-that?p=1543903#post1543903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honstely felt that at this point I knew every single Vampire/Mage/Werewolf/Changeling/Fae power in the game, but I don't recall this &quot;Blessing of the Name&quot;, where can I find information about it? Is it in Clanbook Salubri?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> Clan Book: Salubri p. 44<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T13:14:10-07:00","id":1543906,"title":"","content":"I can see various ways of accomplishing this, in order of ascending difficulty.<br /> <br /> 1) Warp light around the vampire. This is essentially the same principle as making the vampire invisible, which would be a Forces 2/Life 2/Matter 2 spell. Life 2/Matter 2 are locking spheres in this case. The basic principles of light beams and lenses have been around since the 11th century, so this shouldn't be out of reach in the 16th. Downsides: No light reaches the vampire so they are arguably blind unless they have Auspex or the mage incorporates a sensory spell for them.<br /> <br /> 2) Warp just sunlight around the vampire. It's essentially the same spell as in 1, but only warps sunlight. This one depends a lot on what makes sunlight special as the mage will have to be able to discern what counts as sunlight and what doesn't. This may require a lot of research, if it is possible at all. If he can do it, though, this is the same Forces 2/Life 2/Matter 2 just with extra successes required for complexity. Downsides: The vampire will look markedly more shadowy than anyone else nearby.<br /> <br /> 3) Convert all light that approaches the vampire into something else and back again. If the mage can't easily create sunlight (and Mage suggests that they usually can't), he can only convert it back into regular light. This would be Forces 3/Life 2/Matter 2. Downsides: Not much that I can think of mechanically. Narratively there are a lot of ways this could backfire over time.<br /> <br /> 4) A sunlight ward. M20 doesn't have a clear explanation of how to set ward conditions, but I'd recommend Corr 4/Forces 2/[Whatever makes sunlight special] 2 + Life 2/Matter 2 for locking. The Correspondence Ward blocks the light, Forces 2/[Something] 2 defines what light is blocked. Like (2) this will likely require research to properly specify. Downsides: Like in 2, the area around the vampire will look darker than everything else.<br /> <br /> All of this assumes that it is the light and not something that travels with it that injures vampires. If it is actually something light-adjacent, the only one that will work is (4) and then only if the mage can figure out how to identify the light-adjacent thing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T13:30:43-07:00","id":1543907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The new True Black Hand book does suggest something like this is what would happen overtime if magick it's abused to this very end. The Curse mutates if it's foiled creating new weaknesses - it's an interesting way to deal with this sort of things, a bit &quot;party pooper&quot; but not the worst. It defines the Curse as an almost &quot;smart&quot; foe, or at least much more complex than what meets the eye </div> </div> </div>That's in fact what I thought when I was joking with him. The very idea of a Vampire &quot;vulnerable to darkness and shadows&quot; sounds crazy, but at the same time interesting for a change (he would likely avoid Lasombras at all costs lol).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sunligth &quot;immunity&quot; wouldn't be a ward. And that would require to make changes of the Vampires pattern, it's nature. Due to the Cosmological Constants it's justifiable to say it's impossible. </div> </div> </div>Sure, it's just that the player in question was still confused as to what approach to use, but I guess his intention would be more of a pattern change, hence I said it's &quot;a bit too much&quot;, but then he thought of wards, etc. He's more concerned with the ends than with the means, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would say, in any case, that enchanting the vampire itself would cost Permanent Scourge (that rule did exist on Cruzade, if I remember correctly) to the mage while the spell it's active, not unlike raising Atributes above 5 or wanting to be immortal. Having Vulgar stuff that's &quot;always&quot; active it's the kind of thing that justifies this sort of marks - and you ARE raising your middle finger to God, after all. </div> </div> </div>Yes, Sorcerer's Crusade use this system of Permanent Scourge and in this case, IF it's possible at all, at the very least it would cost him that. But to be honest, I'm very reluctant to open such doors...<br /> <br /> My problem with the item approach is that it's just &quot;an easy way out&quot;, to be honest, I think it would be more interesting for the story ramifications to even opt to allow him to be able to make it, but as an unforeseen consequence to make his vampire lover particularly &quot;allergic to darkness&quot;, at least this can lead to interesting (and crazy) stories, it has more potential so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes<br /> Clan Book: Salubri p. 44 </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much, I'll have a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T13:52:54-07:00","id":1543908,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't much of SC's rules, but most of the spells that have been suggested don't enchant anything. They are just spells that travel along with a person, they aren't spells that change or enchant that person.<br /> <br /> Scourge is still a reasonably good way of handling the side effects, but if you don't want that, have the Curse fight back. As others have suggested, it could alter to fit the new normal. Alternatively, it could count as a witness, eroding the spell with Unbelief or even making it Vulgar With Witnesses (if that's an SC thing). You could even use the same scourge rules to represent it fighting back, just have backlashes and other consequences be thematic to the Curse<br /> <br /> Also, for a fun moment. Protecting the vampire from sunlight might not take away Frenzy rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T15:24:47-07:00","id":1543916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could even use the same scourge rules to represent it fighting back, just have backlashes and other consequences be thematic to the Curse </div> </div> </div>Yes, that sounds interesting as well. That's why I mentioned the &quot;weird&quot; allergy to darkness (espeecially more problematic in the 16th century than nowadays, btw), have some weird forms of paradox sounds like a possible good story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T18:05:44-07:00","id":1544366,"title":"","content":"It is doable, but you're essentially trying to subvert the nature of reality. I would ALWAYS consider such effect as a Vain effect, possibly Vain with Witnesses. And as such, apply any sort of fitting scourge shenanigans. This would be pretty much like trying to create a floating castle. Consider even giving the vampire some Permadox (or Perma-Scourge better saying).<br /> <br /> But it should be absolutely doable.<br /> <br /> Just read carefully about any side effects. Magic is not for everyone, consult your Witch-Doctor before using it.","signature":"","edite